      "The Prompt's Stated Premise ('To design the treatment...'): Colleague 5 introduced a powerful translational argument. If a researcher concludes 'Factor B deactivates xy' and designs an inhibitor against B, it fails completely in vivo because ΔB has zero phenotype (5000/ml). Attributing the function to B individually is biologically and clinically invalid.",
