      "How to dismantle: F DOES contain an active falsehood! It asserts that Virulence Factor B is the factor that deactivates xy. But in the intact pathogen, removing B has ZERO effect on xy deactivation. Therefore, B is NOT the factor that deactivates xy in the pathogen—the pathogen's virulence mechanism relies on redundancy. Attributing a complex/redundant phenotype to a single component is a textbook distractor category in competitive biology exams called 'False Specificity / Incomplete Attribution'."
